abstract: >-
  A versioned public research layer for an ongoing inquiry in ecology,
  phenomenology, religion, and creaturely relation. The project includes
  curated Black Walnut field notes, concept pages, methodological
  documentation, sources, and a public record of revision and conceptual
  development over time.

